    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352-a3">

                <pb facs="0624" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg496"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    715.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. St. Victor to Mr. Langston</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State of Foreign Relations</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1885-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 23, 1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: In acknowledging the receipt of
                    your letter of the 12th February, instant, I told you in my dispatch that
                    communication thereof had been made to my colleague of justice.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to transmit to you under this cover copy of his letter of the
                    21st instant, and of that communicated bearing the same date and the No. 17 of
                    the judge of instruction near the civil tribunal of this district, addressed to
                    my colleague.</p>
                <p>These two papers are relative to the affair of d’Almena.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>B. ST. VICTOR.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
